The vulnerability is type CWE-119, complexity Medium, with the following description: '''The getResourceAsStream function in the DefaultClassPathResourceLoader class in the Spring Framework before 5.0.4 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (resource not found) or possibly obtain sensitive information from process memory via a crafted pathname.'''
</s>
The vulnerable lines are:

```java
    public Optional<InputStream> getResourceAsStream(String path) {
        URL url = classLoader.getResource(prefixPath(path));
        if (url == null) {
            return Optional.empty();
        }
        return Optional.of(url.openStream());
    }
```
